$[Import* std]
A splice group `{... a b}` stands for its elements in place; followed by `...` it repeats them together.
$[Macro !rec {{{k v} ...} {. {... k v} ...}}]
${!rec {x 1} {y 2}}
expect: {x: 1, y: 2}
Without `...` a group splices once, and it may hold nested repetitions.
$[Macro !wrap {{x ys ...} {' {... x ys ...} x}}]
${!wrap 0 1 2}
expect: [0, 1, 2, 0]
`!case` expands in one step, so a long or deeply nested match stays within the expansion depth.
${!case {#c {#b 3}} {a x 0} {b x 1} {c x {!case x {a y 0} {b y {* y 2}}}}}
expect: 6
